      "writtenOn": "2024-12-03T19:02:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently the parameter to `GpuTimerCallback` is unsigned, so it can\u0027t be negative. In the current implementations both Ganesh and Graphite will provide a `GpuStats` with 0 for `elapsedTime` so `GpuTimerCallback` will also get a 0.\n\nOnly Graphite provides a `CallbackResult` here. We could force passing 0 to `GpuTimerCallback` if `CallbackResult` is not `kSuccess` in that case (but, as noted above, this is what already happens).\n\nA more radical change could be to modify GpuStats to have an `optional\u003cuint64_t\u003e` so we\ndisambiguate no report from a failed report (and then propagate that to `GpuTimerCallback` in viewer which could draw a line in a different color or something like that on failure).",
